//   2. WRONG ANSWERS (31 examples, mode_F dominant with tiny_span_dominant=94%):
//      Model writes MULTIPLE tiny <<>> spans for intermediate steps; evaluator takes the LAST
//      span which is a partial sub-expression. E.g., model writes <<int(total/n1)>> +
//      <<int((total*t)/n2)>> but the evaluator extracts only the last one.
//      Fix: guidance strongly requires exactly ONE combined final <<expr>> at the END.
//
// Changes from attempt 24:
//   - Guidance: forbid max/min/abs/floor/ceil; require ONE final combined <<expr>>;
//     give multi-variable example; remind about template variable names without braces;
//     explicitly ban intermediate spans.
//   - prefixBudget: 75% (675/900) instead of 78% → 225 steps for constrained phase
//     (vs. 198 steps), giving more budget to close long constrained expressions.
//   - boostAmount: 10.0 (up from 8.0) → stronger soft boost for constrained tokens.
//   - narrowThreshold: 8 (up from 6) → boosting kicks in sooner when grammar narrows.
//
// Rationale stays on GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan because the manual loop in
// attempts 25–26 consistently underperformed this helper (14.3% vs. 34.7% accuracy).
// CSD_RATIONALE_END

// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_BEGIN
// parser_validity: insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//   Initialization: method precondition guarantees insideConstrained ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrained),
//   so the initial assignment is valid. The GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan postcondition
//   directly ensures insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut) and
//   !insideConstrainedOut ==> currentConstrainedOut == []. No additional branches modify
//   constrained state after the helper call, so the invariant is maintained globally.
//   Inside the helper, the free phase entering a constrained span resets currentConstrainedOut
//   to [] (valid) and the forced OpenConstrainedSpan also resets to []; each
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep extends only with parser-valid tokens; CloseConstrainedSpan
//   exits with insideOut=false making the implication vacuously true.
//
// progress: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps, cost <= maxSteps
//   GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan postcondition: |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps.
//   We assign cost := maxSteps satisfying cost <= maxSteps.
//   When maxSteps > 0: cost = maxSteps > 0 directly satisfies the liveness disjunction (cost > 0).
//   Inside the helper, each branch increments the internal step counter: UnconstrainedStep
//   consumes one token-step; OpenConstrainedSpan appends one << token consuming one step;
//   AdaptiveConstrainedStep samples one constrained token; CloseConstrainedSpan appends >>
//   consuming one step. Visible output grows by at most one token per step, so
//   |generated| - |generatedPrefix| <= total_steps_consumed <= maxSteps at all internal points.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END

generated := generatedPrefix;
insideConstrainedOut := insideConstrained;
currentConstrainedOut := currentConstrained;
cost := 0;

if maxSteps == 0 {
  cost := 0;
} else {
  helpers.AppendTaskGuidance(lm, "Solve step by step in plain text. At the very END, write the final answer as exactly ONE <<expr>>. Combine ALL parts of the calculation into this ONE expression. Example: <<int(n * frac_1 * frac_2)>> or <<total // n1 + (total * t) // n2>>. Inside <<>>: variable names without braces (n not {n}, frac_1 not {frac_1}), integers, +, -, *, /, //, %, (, ), int() ONLY. Use // for integer division. FORBIDDEN inside <<>>: max(), min(), abs(), floor(), ceil(), {braces}, $, **, LaTeX, HTML tags, any other functions. Do NOT write multiple <<>> blocks for intermediate steps — ONE final <<expr>> only.");

  var prefixBudget: nat := (maxSteps * 75) / 100;
  if prefixBudget >= maxSteps {
    prefixBudget := maxSteps - 1;
  }

  var g, ic, cc := helpers.GenerateWithPrefixAndManagedSpan(
    lm, parser, prompt, generated, insideConstrainedOut, currentConstrainedOut,
    maxSteps, prefixBudget, validTokenGroups, 10.0, 8, eosToken
  );
  generated := g;
  insideConstrainedOut := ic;
  currentConstrainedOut := cc;

  cost := maxSteps;
